<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">10 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 10 September, from 506 to 1939.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/bishop" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bishop.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">506 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,520 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bishops of Visigothic Gaul meet at the Council of Agde</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With the permission of the Arian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaric-ii">Alaric II</a>, Catholic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> met at Agde and issued canons on clerical discipline, marriage and church property. Many entered later collections of church law.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1089 CE <span class="tih-ago">937 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Urban II opens the Synod of Melfi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-urban-ii">Pope Urban II</a> opened a synod at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/melfi">Melfi</a>, attended by seventy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> and twelve abbots, on church reform and relations with the Greek Church. The Byzantine emperor sent ambassadors, and the Norman duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roger-borsa">Roger Borsa</a> attended in person.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-urban-ii">Pope Urban II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/melfi">Melfi</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1419">1419 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">607 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John the Fearless is murdered on the bridge at Montereau</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> was killed by followers of the Dauphin Charles during peace talks. Burgundy allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, leading to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-troyes">Treaty of Troyes</a> that made Henry V heir to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1509">1509 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">517 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An earthquake in the Sea of Marmara devastates Constantinople</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The earthquake known as Kıyamet-i Suğra, the 'Minor Judgement Day', struck the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-marmara">Sea of Marmara</a> and devastated much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. A tsunami and 45 days of aftershocks followed; estimates of the dead range from 1,000 to 13,000.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-marmara">Sea of Marmara</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1779">1779 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">247 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Pickles captures HMS West Florida on Lake Pontchartrain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a single-ship action on Lake Pontchartrain, then in the British province of West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, the Continental Navy schooner USS Morris fought the British sloop HMS West Florida, which Captain William Pickles boarded and captured.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1813">1813 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">213 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Oliver Hazard Perry wins the Battle of Lake Erie</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matthew-c-perry">Perry</a>'s American squadron captured the entire British force on Lake Erie. His message 'We have met the enemy and they are ours' heralded the recovery of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/detroit">Detroit</a> and the American north-west.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1846">1846 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">180 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Elias Howe patents the lockstitch sewing machine</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Elias Howe received a US patent for a machine using an eye-pointed needle and a shuttle to form a lockstitch. He later won royalties from Singer and other makers who used his design.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1939">1939 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">87 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Canada declares war on Germany</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A week after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>'s parliament declared war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in its own right. More than a million Canadians served in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a></div></div></li></ol>
